Package: cursor-speak
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Brian Perry <perry.brian@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, python3-venv, speech-dispatcher | espeak-ng, pipewire-bin | pulseaudio-utils | alsa-utils
Recommends: libnotify-bin, wl-clipboard, ydotool
Description: Reads new Cursor CLI replies out loud
 Cursor Speak sits in the system tray, watches your Cursor CLI (cursor-agent)
 chats, and reads each finished reply out loud. Code blocks, commands, file
 paths and tool output are left out; headings and bullets are read as plain
 sentences.
 .
 Voice: a local piper neural voice, downloaded per user on first run into
 ~/.local/share/cursor-speak (about 80 MB, nothing is bundled in this package),
 with espeak-ng or speech-dispatcher as a fallback. Chat files are only ever
 opened read-only.
 .
 Voice input: press a keyboard shortcut, talk, and your words go to a new
 cursor-agent session or are typed into the focused window (ydotool). Speech is
 recognised on your computer with faster-whisper (downloaded per user on first
 use, about 200 MB); no cloud speech service is used.
